From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glats <glats@local>
Date: 2026-06-24
Subject: [PATCH] settings: allow non-flatpak callers for Settings.Read

xdg-desktop-portal 1.20.x introduced an authorization callback that resolves
the caller's app ID via /proc/PID/root/.flatpak-info. For non-flatpak apps
(e.g. native Nautilus on Hyprland), this lookup fails and the portal denies
the request with "Access denied: Unable to open /proc/PID/root".

The Settings.Read / ReadAll methods don't need caller authentication — they
just query the backend implementation. Allow Settings calls without resolving
the caller's app info.

See: https://github.com/flatpak/xdg-desktop-portal/issues/1752
---
 src/xdg-desktop-portal.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/xdg-desktop-portal.c b/src/xdg-desktop-portal.c
index 45df252..e851493 100644
--- a/src/xdg-desktop-portal.c
+++ b/src/xdg-desktop-portal.c
@@ -119,6 +119,19 @@ authorize_callback (GDBusInterfaceSkeleton *interface,
                     GDBusMethodInvocation  *invocation,
                     gpointer                user_data)
 {
+  /* The Settings interface doesn't require caller authentication.
+     Non-flatpak apps (e.g. native Nautilus on Hyprland) need to read
+     color-scheme via the portal, but xdp_invocation_ensure_app_info_sync
+     fails for non-sandboxed processes. Skip the check for Settings. */
+  if (g_strcmp0 (g_dbus_method_invocation_get_interface_name (invocation),
+                 "org.freedesktop.portal.Settings") == 0)
+    return TRUE;
+
   g_autoptr(XdpAppInfo) app_info = NULL;
   g_autoptr(GError) error = NULL;
 
